      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Just to be clear for anyone looking into this, the other keys work fine?\n\nIn english I think the controls are \"wasd\", and from your post I think we can infer two letters \"zq??\". \n\nLooking at an image (calling out what I did in case I'm wrong) I get \"zqsd\"\n\nMapping keys can be fun times because OS translates from position to key, and in some cases a program might to translate back to key location.\n\nTry wasd to see where things are. W should be opposite movement to S. A will be opposite of D. You've reported what Q does, so also test Z. \n\nI guess mapping can get tricky if some things are by letter and then try to squeeze in wasd equivalent.",
